      "en": "Between the two there is certainly room theoretically for psychological functions. But we see at once that properly psychological functions will always tend to be interpreted either in relation to vital functions or in relation to social functions, so that their autonomy will remain precarious and their specificity contested. In this sense Comte, helped by his total incomprehension of psychological reality, showed a kind of divination in refusing to assign a place to psychology in the classification of the sciences."
