      "en": "When in Claudel's play The City the pessimist Besme declares that 'nothing is,' he means precisely that to this analysis, to this test, no experience resists. It will always be around death considered precisely as exposure, as evidence of this ultimate nothingness, that this kind of inverted apologetics constituting absolute pessimism will gravitate."
